# Push to main

Do not ask whether to commit or push. When a task is finished:

1. Create a git commit on `main` (or the current branch if it is already `main`).
2. Push to `origin` with `git push -u origin HEAD` if needed.

Still follow git safety: no force-push, no `--no-verify`, no amending published commits unless the user explicitly asks.
